1871, 632, 1460], "window": [8483, 37283], "confidence": 0.62, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Ignoring time, 1885 reaches 1460 by exactly one route: 1885->749->1453->1871->632->1460 (the 1572->826 branch dead-ends). Under the 600-unit relay constraint this 5-hop chain must complete within ~2400 time units. However 1885 emits only 5 events across the 28.8k window, each in a separate sub-window with no burst, 1460 has just 4 in-events peaking in different sub-windows than 632, and the six chain nodes together produce only ~36 low-degree, evenly-spread events (<=6 per 2400-unit bin). No temporally compressed relay is possible. The large global event volume and the existence of a static path are the confounders here and are explicitly controlled for."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structural reachability (time ignored).** Forward search from 1885 and backward search from 1460:\n\n- 1885 \u2192 {749, 1572} (step_04)\n- 749 \u2192 {1453} only; 1572 \u2192 {826} only (step_06, step_07)\n- 1453 \u2192 {221, 1280, 1396, 1871}; 826 \u2192 {676, 1580} \u2014 the 1572 branch dead-ends away from 1460 (step_11, step_12)\n- 1460 \u2190 {632, 765, 1045} (step_05); 632 \u2190 {161, 1184, 1871} (step_08); 765 \u2190 {149,1081,1132,1210,1382} (step_09); 1045 \u2190 {981,1682,1992} (step_10)\n\nThe **only** static route is the 5-hop chain `1885 \u2192 749 \u2192 1453 \u2192 1871 \u2192 632 \u2192 1460`. There is no shorter path, and no alternate branch.\n\n**Temporal feasibility.** A valid cascade would need 5 strictly increasing events with each gap \u2264 600, i.e. the whole chain compressed into \u2264 2400 time units inside a 28,800-unit window. But:\n\n- 1885 fires only 5 events in the entire window (step_02), scattered across widely separated sub-windows (step_15: one event each around 15.7k\u201319.3k, 19.3k\u201322.9k, two around 30k\u201333.7k, one after 33.7k) \u2014 no dense burst.\n- 1460 has only 4 in-events (step_02), and 1460/632 activity peaks in different sub-windows (step_16).\n- All six chain nodes combined generate ~36 events spread evenly over twelve 2400-unit bins, never more than 6 in any bin (step_13, step_14) \u2014 far too diffuse for a five-link chain to align inside one 2400-unit span.\n\n**Confounder controls.** The graph is large and busy (5,905 events, 1,917 active nodes, repeat_ratio 0.0135 \u2014 step_01), so raw volume alone would falsely suggest connectivity; and a static path *does* exist. Both of these are exactly the insufficient signals warned about. The chain nodes are also low-degree (6\u20139 events each, step_14), not hubs, so \"popularity\" does not supply the missing timing either.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_82bdb271\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 749, 1453, 1871, 632, 1460],\n  \"window\": [8483, 37283],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Ignoring time, 1885 reaches 1460 by exactly one route: 1885->749->1453->1871->632->1460 (the 1572->826 branch dead-ends). Under the 600-unit relay constraint this 5-hop chain must complete within ~2400 time units. However 1885 emits only 5 events across the 28.8k window, each in a separate sub-window with no burst, 1460 has just 4 in-events peaking in different sub-windows than 632, and the six chain nodes together produce only ~36 low-degree, evenly-spread events (<=6 per 2400-unit bin). No temporally compressed relay is possible. The large global event volume and the existence of a static path are the confounders here and are explicitly controlled for.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 41247, "total_output_tokens": 6277, "total_tokens": 47524, "total_latency_ms": 86027, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}